Now I have the full picture. Here's the answer:

The JSONL agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Factory AI Droid) share a **similar** shape but differ in specific fields. Here's what each line looks like in `full.jsonl`:

**Claude Code:**
```json
{"type":"user","uuid":"u1","timestamp":"...","parentUuid":"","cwd":"/repo","sessionId":"sess-1","version":"1","gitBranch":"main","message":{"content":"hello"},"toolUseResult":{...}}
{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"...","requestId":"req-1","message":{"id":"msg-1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"..."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"tu-1","name":"Bash","input":{...},"caller":"..."}]}}
{"type":"progress","message":{...}}
{"type":"file-history-snapshot","files":[...]}
{"type":"system","message":{...}}
```

**Cursor** — same shape but uses `role` instead of `type`:
```json
{"role":"user","timestamp":"...","message":{"content":"hello"}}
{"role":"assistant","timestamp":"...","message":{"content":[...]}}
```

**Factory AI Droid** — wraps everything in an envelope:
```json
{"type":"message","id":"m1","timestamp":"t1","message":{"role":"user","content":[...]}}
{"type":"message","id":"m2","timestamp":"t2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[...]}}
{"type":"session_start","id":"...","title":"..."}
```

**Gemini CLI** — can appear in two shapes. Native format has no `message` wrapper:
```json
{"type":"user","content":[{"text":"hello"}]}
{"type":"gemini","id":"g1","content":"string or array"}
```

**Copilot CLI** — completely different event-based structure (and `Compact()` has **no tests for it** — it's not handled by compact.go at all).

So to directly answer your question: **no, there's no unified structure for the raw `full.jsonl` files.** The differences are:

| Field | Claude Code | Cursor | Factory AI Droid | Gemini |
|-------|------------|--------|-----------------|--------|
| Role indicator | `type` | `role` | `message.role` (inside envelope) | `type` (uses "gemini" not "assistant") |
| Message wrapper | `message: {...}` | `message: {...}` | `message: {role, content}` inside `type:"message"` envelope | Optional — can be top-level or nested |
| Extra line types | `progress`, `file-history-snapshot`, `system` | none observed | `session_start`, `session_event` | none observed |
| User content | string or `[{type, text}]` blocks | string or blocks | string or blocks (inside envelope) | `[{text:"..."}]` array |
| Claude-specific fields | `uuid`, `parentUuid`, `cwd`, `sessionId`, `gitBranch`, `toolUseResult`, `requestId` | none of these | `id` on envelope | `id` at top level |

`Compact()` normalizes Claude/Cursor/Factory/Gemini into a unified output format, but Copilot CLI appears to be missing from that pipeline entirely.

